.TITLE "du"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Estimates file and directory space usage. It is used to identify which __folders__ or __files__ are consuming the most space on your disk.

.DIV "TLDR"
**du path**
Displays the space usage for a directory and all its subdirectories.
> __path__ the target directory

**du -h path**
Displays the space usage in human-readable formats like GB or MB.
> __-h__ human-readable flag | __path__ the target directory

**du -s -h path**
Displays only a summary of the total size for a specific path.
> __-s__ summary flag | __-h__ human-readable flag | __path__ target path

**du -a -h path**
Includes individual files in the output instead of just directories.
> __-a__ all files flag | __-h__ human-readable flag | __path__ target path

**du -h --max-depth=1 path**
Shows the size of immediate subdirectories without showing every nested folder.
> __-h__ human-readable flag | __--max-depth=1__ depth limit | __path__ target

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Combining __du -s -h__ with a wildcard (e.g., __du -s -h *__) is an excellent way to see the size of everything in your current folder. This tool is essential for cleaning up storage and finding "space hogs."

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:df** **cli:ls** **cli:ncdu**

documentation: __https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/du__
